[Evidence Curator] (Seq: CAFWKTCE)
  [Evidence Curator]
  Sequence CAFWKTCE contains the FWKT pharmacophore (Phe-Trp-Lys-Thr), the master-key motif for SSTR2 binding. Per PDB 7T10 (SSTR2-somatostatin complex):
  - Trp indole ring inserts into the TM3-TM7 hydrophobic pocket (Phe6.52/Phe7.35 stacking).
  - Lys forms a critical salt bridge with Asp3.32 on TM3.
  - Disulfide bond Cys(0)-Cys(6) (ring size: 5 residues) constrains the peptide into a beta-turn, mimicking the bioactive conformation of octreotide.
  This structural arrangement is consistent with Weckbecker et al. (Nat Rev Drug Discov, 2003).

